A||||13||2M4 Dale||Duke to V6 swap questions ???||||5||
Z||000000||2M4 Dale||01-04-2001||08:36 AM||||OK.......I got this 88 V6 and I want to put it into my 87 coupe. I plan on using the intake, plenum, distributor, wiring, air box, etc. from a 85 GT to do the swap. Will I encounter any problems with the 88 engine and the 85 parts car as far as compatability ?<P>Also....My 87 has the 5 spd Izusu tranny. Will this mate up to / work OK with a mildly hopped up V6...should I have the tranny overhauled first ? It works OK behind the Duke but it does have 106,000 miles on it. And what clutch-pressure plate should I use ? I understand that there is something different about the 88's flywheel. <P>Exhaust...my coupe has the single cutout for the exhaust tips. I would like to keep it that way....kinda keep it looking like a 2M4..."sleeper". Will my 4 cylinder exhaust (cat back) work with the V6 or will I have to have something custom made ?<P>And one more thing ... will my speedo and dash gages work OK as is, provided I use a V6-5spd. ECM ? Or will I have to go with a V6 dash gage assembly ?||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||01-04-2001||11:05 AM||||I don't know if 85 wiring is the same but I do know 86-88 will plug right in.<BR>The izusu 5 is sweet I like it better than the getrag<BR>look at <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004793.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/004793.html</A> <BR>and <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-003491.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20001206-2-003491.html</A> <P>------------------<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||01-04-2001||11:43 AM||||Which engine harness will you be using? More to the point, which alternator? The '88 alternator plug is different but the mounting is the same. Use whichever alternator for the plug.<P>On the clutch/pressure plate, off hand I'd have to say to use the one for the transmission but I'm unsure that the pressure plate will bolt to the '88 flywheel. Ogre?<P>Use the 'Y' pipe's drop tube to the converter , cut and modify the 4 cylinder exhaust there. Everything should be in line at that point. I would look into a flowmaster muffler to replace the original.<P>On the gauges, you will need to modify the tach resistor so it will read correctly, or swap clusters (thats what I would do), there should be a plug already in your car's harness to accept the center gauge cluster.||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||01-04-2001||12:58 PM||||Dale, call me here at the shop and we can fill you in on all you need -- we do this swap quite often...........510-233-4376 -- also watch your email about the other parts.....||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||01-04-2001||03:25 PM|||| Dont forget to change the radateor 6 has double core my 88 cracted its head with singe core 4cly in it.i didnt do swap got it that way.||||reg||1
Z||000005||TheFiero64||01-04-2001||04:03 PM||||all fiero's have the same radiator. It only differs standard & auto because of the trans cooler. You must have had an aftermarket radiator. My 88 has the original radiator and it runs really cool.||||reg||1
Z||000006||2M4 Dale||01-05-2001||12:07 AM||||ray b.....I have checked the parts numbers on that radiator deal and the only differance I can find is between manual and auto....the trans cooler must be the second core that your thinking of. I've also heard that the stainless steel tubes are different...any one know ?<P>Indiana...I'm gonna use the 85 GT parts cars wiring harness. And so I guess the 85 alternator. As far as the exhaust goes...I'm thinking Fiero Store headers and a local muffler shop that does custom bending with a good aftermarket muffler. And I'll probably be looking for a 120 speedo gage package to replace my unit......But I really don't want the auxillary gages...(I think that they just add to that "attack of the pod people" look that the Fiero interior aready has...lol) ..how am I gonna do that ?.....lol<P>64....I will stick with my ultra smoooooth Izusu I believe....I'll probably just have it gone thru.<P>Terry.....I will give you a call at the FieroShop when I actually get a little closer to doing the deed on my car....this coming FALL  :-(  <BR>And I will get in touch with you about the parts we have discused via email....I want all three parts.....pick me out some nice ones and lay them aside, if you would, it's gonna take me about two weeks to get the cash.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ray b||01-05-2001||02:19 PM|||| 64 and dale NO NOT same radiator v6 is thicker 2 rows 4cly is 1 row. numbers can lie, check out this post <A HREF="http://www.fieroforum/forum2/html/006894" TARGET=_blank>www.fieroforum/forum2/html/006894</A>   on 11-21-2000 by archie+ mr fiero you be sorry if you cook it. archie and others have v6 rads stacked up as takeouts for 4cores for v8s.<BR>I learn the hard way.    ray||||reg||1
